IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), sections 12 to 16 -- THE DEATH OF A
-- BENEFICIARY, AND REPRESENTATIVES.
--
-- "Representative" is not defined in the Regulations (it is borrowed from the law of Canada
-- or of a province), so who is one is asked as a fact.

§ `Regulations s 12 -- Notice to Minister`

DECLARE `Relationship to a deceased beneficiary` IS ONE OF
    `executor or administrator of the estate`
    `liquidator of the succession`
    `heir`
    `none of these`

-- 12: the duty to tell the Minister, as soon as feasible. The text sets no day, so the rule
-- says only whether the duty has arisen for a person.
-- src:170 | 12 If a beneficiary dies, the executor or administrator of the estate, the liquidator of the succession or the beneficiary’s heirs must, as soon as feasible, notify the Minister of the beneficiary’s death.
@ref Regulations s 12 (src:170)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relationship to the beneficiary` IS A `Relationship to a deceased beneficiary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` `the beneficiary has died` `relationship to the beneficiary` MEANS
        `the beneficiary has died`
    AND (CONSIDER `relationship to the beneficiary`
         WHEN `executor or administrator of the estate` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `liquidator of the succession`            THEN TRUE
         WHEN `heir`                                    THEN TRUE
         WHEN `none of these`                           THEN FALSE)

§ `Regulations s 13 -- Payment to estate, succession or heirs`

-- 13(1): the estate, succession or heirs are eligible for the allocation payment for the
-- month of death if the beneficiary did not receive it.
-- src:172 | 13 (1) If a beneficiary dies, the beneficiary’s estate or succession or the beneficiary’s heirs are eligible to receive an allocation payment for the month in which the beneficiary died if the beneficiary did not receive the allocation payment for that month.
@ref Regulations s 13(1) (src:172)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary received the allocation payment for the month in which they died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the estate or succession or the heirs are eligible to receive the allocation payment for the month of death` `the beneficiary has died` `the beneficiary received the allocation payment for the month in which they died` MEANS
        `the beneficiary has died`
    AND NOT `the beneficiary received the allocation payment for the month in which they died`

-- 13(2): an amount owing on the death, or a payment returned to the Minister after it, goes
-- to the estate or succession or the heirs; if there are no heirs, to a person or agency the
-- Minister designates.
-- src:174 | (2) Any amount owing as a benefit on the death of the beneficiary, or any benefit paid to the beneficiary or on their behalf in accordance with the Act and these Regulations but returned to the Minister after the death of a beneficiary, must be paid to the beneficiary’s estate or succession or the beneficiary’s heirs. If there are no heirs, this amount must be paid to a person or agency designated by the Minister.
@ref Regulations s 13(2) (src:174)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has heirs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Recipient of an amount owing on a death`
`who receives an amount owing on the death of a beneficiary` `the beneficiary has heirs` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiary has heirs`
    THEN `the beneficiary's estate or succession or the beneficiary's heirs`
    ELSE `a person or agency designated by the Minister`

§ `Regulations s 14 -- Presumption of death`

-- 14(1): the Minister may fix a date of presumed death if the beneficiary has disappeared
-- in circumstances the Minister concludes raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption
-- of death.
-- src:176 | 14 (1) If a beneficiary has disappeared under circumstances that the Minister concludes raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that the beneficiary is dead, the Minister may determine the date on which, for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations, that beneficiary’s death is presumed to have occurred, and the beneficiary will be deemed for all purposes of the Act and these Regulations to have died on that date.
@ref Regulations s 14(1) (src:176)
GIVEN `the beneficiary has disappeared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister concludes that the circumstances raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that the beneficiary is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may determine the date on which the beneficiary's death is presumed to have occurred` `the beneficiary has disappeared` `the Minister concludes that the circumstances raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that the beneficiary is dead` MEANS
        `the beneficiary has disappeared`
    AND `the Minister concludes that the circumstances raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that the beneficiary is dead`

-- 14(1) and 14(2): the beneficiary is deemed to have died on the date the Minister
-- determined, which the Minister may later change; if there is no determination the date is
-- the actual one (NOTHING when neither is known).
@ref Regulations s 14(1) and (2) (src:176) (src:178)
GIVEN `the date the Minister determined as the presumed date of death` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the actual date of death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date of death for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` `the date the Minister determined as the presumed date of death` `the actual date of death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the Minister determined as the presumed date of death`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the actual date of death`

-- 14(2) and 14(3): when the Minister is satisfied on new information or evidence that the
-- date of death is different (and fixes a different date) or that the beneficiary is alive,
-- the Minister must pay, within a reasonable time, any benefit that would have been payable
-- had the first determination not been made.
-- src:178 | (2) If, after having determined the date of the beneficiary’s death, the Minister is satisfied on the basis of new information or evidence that the date of death is different, the Minister may determine a different date for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations and the Minister must, within a reasonable time, pay any benefit that would have been payable if the initial determination had not been made.
-- src:179 | Beneficiary is alive
-- src:180 | (3) If, after having determined the date of the beneficiary’s death under this section, the Minister is satisfied on the basis of new information or evidence that the beneficiary is alive, the Minister must, within a reasonable time, pay any benefit that would have been payable to the beneficiary had that determination not been made.
@ref Regulations s 14(2) and (3) (src:178-180)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a different date of death on the basis of new information or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied on the basis of new information or evidence that the beneficiary is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must pay any benefit that would have been payable had the first determination not been made` `the Minister has determined a different date of death on the basis of new information or evidence` `the Minister is satisfied on the basis of new information or evidence that the beneficiary is alive` MEANS
        `the Minister has determined a different date of death on the basis of new information or evidence`
     OR `the Minister is satisfied on the basis of new information or evidence that the beneficiary is alive`

§ `Regulations ss 15 and 16 -- Representatives`

-- 15: a representative may act for a person incapable of managing their own affairs, in any
-- application, statement, notice, request for reconsideration or appeal under the Act or the
-- Regulations.
-- src:186 | 15 If a person is incapable of managing their own affairs, their representative may act on their behalf, including by making any application, statement, notice, request for reconsideration or appeal referred to in the Act or these Regulations.
@ref Regulations s 15 (src:186)
GIVEN `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is that person's representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the representative may act on the person's behalf` `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` `the other person is that person's representative` MEANS
        `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs`
    AND `the other person is that person's representative`

-- 16: the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid to the representative, if the
-- beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs and the representative is authorized
-- by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage them.
-- src:188 | 16 If a beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs, the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on their behalf to their representative, if the representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary’s affairs.
@ref Regulations s 16 (src:188)
GIVEN `the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on the beneficiary's behalf to their representative` `the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs` `the representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs` MEANS
        `the beneficiary is incapable of managing their own affairs`
    AND `the representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the beneficiary's affairs`
